G2 script T1: Corv IH->Ind 22-43 (targets Ind directly, so FollowMe is useless); Drag PROTECT blocks Hurr and denies a Pelipper Protect-read on early SW. Save SW for T2 when Pelipper commits.</think><tool_call>execute<arg_key>code</arg_key><arg_value>// T1 cross-checks before committing to the G2 script: Corv IH->Ind + Drag Protect.
// Questions: (1) Pelipper Hurr into Dragalge if Protect somehow fails / is ignored;
// (2) IH->Ind chip range with Ind's +1 SpD (Seed) — physical, so SpD boost shouldn't matter;
// (3) order sanity: does Corv outspeed Ind/Pel here, and could Ind TR first?
const [hurrDrag, ihInd, order1, order2] = await Promise.all([
  tools.estimate_damage({ attacker: "Pelipper", defender: "Dragalge", move: "Hurricane" }),
  tools.estimate_damage({ attacker: "Corviknight", defender: "Indeedee-F", move: "Iron Head" }),
  tools.compare_action_order({ first: "Corviknight", second: "Indeedee-F", first_move: "Iron Head", second_move: "FollowMe" }),
  tools.compare_action_order({ first: "Dragalge", second: "Pelipper", first_move: "Protect", second_move: "Hurricane" })
]);
return { hurrDrag, ihInd, order1, order2 };
